    <article class="project-narrative">
      <div class="project-overview" data-scroll-group data-scroll-step="80">
        <p class="lede">At PwC, I worked on an AI platform that could support two sides of IT operations. It could answer technical questions from a maintained body of evidence, and it could carry out service tickets inside the browser where an operator already had access to the relevant business applications.</p>
        <p>A request to give a colleague access might require finding the right account, changing its permissions, and stopping for multi-factor authentication. A question about a broken application might first expose a gap in the available guidance. I built two connected parts around those needs. <strong>Knowledge Management</strong> uses AI to identify missing questions, group related gaps into research objectives, find authoritative starting pages, and steer focused crawling towards useful evidence. <strong>Browser Control</strong> lets an operator hand a natural-language ticket to an AI agent, watch it work in a separate browser tab, and intervene whenever human judgement or authentication is needed.</p>
